Driver end-to-end on this fixture: tools/rustle_pipeline.sh's candidates and assign stages (spec 2026-10-02 §7).

  bash tools/rlock.sh heavy bash tests/fixtures/o3_candidates/driver/run_e2e.sh --bin <CARGO_TARGET_DIR>/release --out <scratch>

run_e2e.sh builds the families stage's three products from the fixture (the fixture has no O1 products: its one locus
gives the families stage no family): fx.fam.copies.tsv/.fa = the fixture's copy table (MCL0, copy A) plus a control family
MCL1 without a candidate (one copy at chrT:30000-30500, n_reads 0), and fx.fam.copies.regions in mcl_families' layout
(hull +- 5 kb). It runs the driver's candidates and assign stages, and assign --no-candidates on the same inputs, then
checks, exiting non-zero at the first failure it names:
  (a) placement by the patch realignment: the 60 copy-B reads (B_*, the generator's names) have their primaries on
      cand_MCL0_0 at MAPQ >= 60 in fx.aug.bam; the 60 copy-A reads' primaries are those of the fixture BAM
  (b) MCL0 is assigned as a 2-copy family that includes cand_MCL0_0 (families.tsv n_copies 2, quant.tsv lists it), with
      the AS-tied gate at its default (ratio 1.00)
  (c) the control family's tables are the same in the split and in the --no-candidates run (MCL1 has no reads: this checks
      the split's selection, regions and concatenation)

Ruling R13 (2026-10-02): O2's scope is AS-tied molecules (assign-or-abstain). A read that the realignment places uniquely
on a candidate is placed by the aligner and never enters the certificate. So fx.assign.assignments.tsv holds no MCL0 row
on this fixture, with or without the candidate: every molecule is a clear-best mapper. That is the intended behaviour, not
a gap. The candidate's reads are the 60 copy-B primaries on cand_MCL0_0 in fx.aug.bam.

Seen 2026-10-02 (minimap2 2.30-r1287, samtools 1.22.1): all assertions hold. The driver reports 1 flagged candidate;
fx.aug.bam has 120 primary records, 60 of them on cand_MCL0_0; assign gives 0 rows. The flag stage, run with a one-gene
GFF (chrT 10001-13100 geneA), gives geneA o3_candidate = cand_MCL0_0.
